{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 413 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "c709209493700d8d4d4b86810d5f7d72252012c1afb547d54162ea83907719e2" :edb/db-before-t 412 :edb/db-after-t 413 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533725 50 #inst "2026-10-04T19:24:04.876Z" 13194139533725 true] [17592186059572 1020 #edb/ref 17592186248642 13194139533725 true] [17592186068681 1020 #edb/ref 17592186248628 13194139533725 true] [17592186073753 1020 #edb/ref 17592186248649 13194139533725 true] [17592186083147 1020 #edb/ref 17592186248625 13194139533725 true] [17592186083302 1020 #edb/ref 17592186248622 13194139533725 true] [17592186087708 1020 #edb/ref 17592186248635 13194139533725 true] [17592186088193 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533725 true] [17592186088193 1145 "First, we write the equation in standard form by bringing all of the terms to the left-hand side. This gives the equation\n\n$$\n3{x}^{2}-6x+4=0.\n$$\n\nWe can find the roots of a quadratic equation using the quadratic formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the coefficients are $a=3,\\,b=-6,$ and $c=4.$ Substituting these values into the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{-(-6)\\pm \\sqrt{(-6{)}^{2}-4(3)(4)}}{2(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\pm \\sqrt{36-48}}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\pm \\sqrt{-12}}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\pm 2\\sqrt{-3}}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}}{6} \\\\  & =1\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has two solutions, $x=1+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\,\\text{i}$ and $x=1-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\,\\text{i}.$" 13194139533725 true] [17592186192640 1020 #edb/ref 17592186248615 13194139533725 true] [17592186248615 1017 #edb/ref 17592186248616 13194139533725 true] [17592186248615 1089 "q-148499" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248615 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533725 true] [17592186248615 1100 "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=\\frac{3x+1}{x-4}.$" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248615 1113 #uuid "14eca034-3075-5295-bbf9-c2a9d6845c19" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248615 1138 false 13194139533725 true] [17592186248615 1145 "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{3x+1}{x-4}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{3y+1}{y-4}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{3y+1}{y-4} \\\\ x(y-4) & =3y+1 \\\\ xy-4x & =3y+1 \\\\ xy-3y & =4x+1 \\\\ y(x-3) & =4x+1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{4x+1}{x-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{4x+1}{x-3}.\n$$" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248616 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248617 13194139533725 true] [17592186248616 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248618 13194139533725 true] [17592186248616 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248619 13194139533725 true] [17592186248616 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248620 13194139533725 true] [17592186248616 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248621 13194139533725 true] [17592186248616 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533725 true] [17592186248616 1041 "selection" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248616 1104 #edb/ref 17592186248618 13194139533725 true] [17592186248616 1110 #uuid "51772b94-4ac5-5441-ba79-17a300fdbe73" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248617 1034 "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{4x+3}{x-1}" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248617 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533725 true] [17592186248617 1111 #uuid "ebee1fca-7700-5f76-84e3-76f02471e513" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248618 1034 "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{4x+1}{x-3}" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248618 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533725 true] [17592186248618 1111 #uuid "99d09ff5-f710-59af-b3df-bbb614071ce4" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248619 1034 "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x+3}{4x-1}" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248619 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533725 true] [17592186248619 1111 #uuid "5dcf625f-0587-5cff-8876-293e9175ff61" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248620 1034 "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{3x+4}{x-1}" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248620 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533725 true] [17592186248620 1111 #uuid "593c60d5-c90c-5383-8421-33b53b130d16" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248621 1034 "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x+1}{x-3}" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248621 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533725 true] [17592186248621 1111 #uuid "1e966ec0-c646-548f-8299-d6348ce45289" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248622 1017 #edb/ref 17592186248623 13194139533725 true] [17592186248622 1089 "q-288831" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248622 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533725 true] [17592186248622 1100 "The quadratic coefficient of a particular quadratic equation equals $7.$ The sum of the solutions equals $9,$ and the product of the solutions equals $15.$ Find the equation.\n\nThe equation is\n{{field-1}}\n$=0.$" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248622 1113 #uuid "ac82d650-d498-5c2d-b6c5-f429a5e6935c" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248622 1138 false 13194139533725 true] [17592186248622 1145 "Suppose the quadratic equation\n\n$$\na{x}^{2}+bx+c=0\n$$\n\nhas the solutions $x={x}_{1}$ and $x={x}_{2},$ where $a\\ne 0.$ \n\nThen, Vieta's formulas state the following:\n\n- The sum of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-\\frac{b}{a}.\n$$\n\n- The product of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{c}{a}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's use the given information to determine the values of $a,b,$ and $c$ in this case:\n\n- We're told that the quadratic coefficient equals $7.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\na=7.\n$$\n\n- We're told that the sum of the roots equals $9.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9 & =-\\frac{b}{a} \\\\ 9 & =-\\frac{b}{7} \\\\ -63 & =b \\\\ b & =-63.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- We're told that the product of the roots equals $15.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15 & =\\frac{c}{a} \\\\ 15 & =\\frac{c}{7} \\\\ 105 & =c \\\\ c & =105.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation has coefficients\n\n$$\na=7,\\,b=-63,\\,c=105\n$$\n\nand the equation is\n\n$$\n7{x}^{2}-63x+105=0.\n$$" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248623 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248624 13194139533725 true] [17592186248623 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533725 true] [17592186248623 1041 "field-1" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248623 1104 #edb/ref 17592186248624 13194139533725 true] [17592186248623 1110 #uuid "0a098b23-9d0e-5164-984c-50233969cbd7" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248624 1034 "7x^2-63x+105" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248624 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533725 true] [17592186248624 1111 #uuid "5741475c-487a-5222-9fcb-362425da2dad" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248625 1017 #edb/ref 17592186248626 13194139533725 true] [17592186248625 1089 "q-323219" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248625 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533725 true] [17592186248625 1100 "According to the rational root theorem, the polynomial $f(x)=-23{x}^{4}+6{x}^{3}-8x+23$ has{{field-1}} *potential* rational roots." 13194139533725 true] [17592186248625 1113 #uuid "fa1a6f51-b1cf-50d7-b101-ca935fbe5b81" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248625 1138 false 13194139533725 true] [17592186248625 1145 "Given a polynomial with integer coefficients, the rational roots theorem states that any rational roots of the polynomial must take the form\n\n$$\n\\pm \\frac{\\text{factor of the constant term}}{\\text{factor of the leading coefficient}}.\n$$\n\nFor the given polynomial:\n\n- The constant term is $23,$ and its factors are $\\pm 1$ and $\\pm 23.$\n\n- The leading coefficient is $-23,$ and its factors are $\\pm 1$ and $\\pm 23.$\n\nFirst, we list out all the possibilities for the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pm \\frac{1}{1}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{23}, \\\\ \\pm \\frac{23}{1}, & \\pm \\frac{23}{23}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we reduce the fractions to lowest terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pm 1, & \\pm \\frac{1}{23}, \\\\ \\pm 23, & \\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that some potential roots are duplicates (shown above in red). Removing these duplicates, and listing those remaining in order from least to greatest in absolute value, we have\n\n$$\n\\pm \\frac{1}{23},\\,\\pm 1,\\,\\pm 23.\n$$\n\nThis makes a total of $6$ potential roots. (Remember that each $\\pm $ sign accounts for $2$ roots, and $2\\cdot 3=6.$)" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248626 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248627 13194139533725 true] [17592186248626 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533725 true] [17592186248626 1041 "field-1" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248626 1104 #edb/ref 17592186248627 13194139533725 true] [17592186248626 1110 #uuid "fbdd7886-766c-568e-92c6-936e08ae1370" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248627 1034 "6" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248627 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533725 true] [17592186248627 1111 #uuid "6b96f9dd-34fd-544e-bb7f-e0f24b713bf0" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248628 1017 #edb/ref 17592186248629 13194139533725 true] [17592186248628 1089 "q-41570" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248628 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533725 true] [17592186248628 1100 "Simplify $\\frac{5a-2}{a-7}-\\frac{3a+5}{7-a}.$" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248628 1113 #uuid "b9db0d51-60e0-519e-a859-b977ba7429f8" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248628 1138 false 13194139533725 true] [17592186248628 1145 "In order to subtract the two fractions, we need them to have a common denominator. Here, we can put both fractions over a common denominator of $a-7$ if we multiply the top and bottom of the second fraction by $-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5a-2}{a-7}-\\frac{3a+5}{7-a} & = \\\\ \\frac{5a-2}{a-7}-\\frac{(-1)}{(-1)}\\cdot \\frac{3a+5}{7-a} & = \\\\ \\frac{5a-2}{a-7}+\\frac{3a+5}{a-7} & = \\\\ \\frac{(5a-2)+(3a+5)}{a-7} & = \\\\ \\frac{5a-2+3a+5}{a-7} & = \\\\ \\frac{8a+3}{a-7} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248630 13194139533725 true] [17592186248629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248631 13194139533725 true] [17592186248629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248632 13194139533725 true] [17592186248629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248633 13194139533725 true] [17592186248629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248634 13194139533725 true] [17592186248629 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533725 true] [17592186248629 1041 "selection" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248629 1104 #edb/ref 17592186248633 13194139533725 true] [17592186248629 1110 #uuid "8d2200f0-f3d6-5626-aef5-3afff9c0de6e" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248630 1034 "\\frac{8a-7}{a-7}" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248630 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533725 true] [17592186248630 1111 #uuid "8ad55c21-9223-5a4b-ac5d-5130e8248d20" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248631 1034 "\\frac{2a-7}{a-7}" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248631 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533725 true] [17592186248631 1111 #uuid "63dcfe6a-62a8-5e44-af92-920d65146c97" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248632 1034 "\\frac{8a+7}{a-7}" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248632 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533725 true] [17592186248632 1111 #uuid "fca1bd70-4f9f-5c21-a999-6e7d7b1a4c44" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248633 1034 "\\frac{8a+3}{a-7}" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248633 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533725 true] [17592186248633 1111 #uuid "18d35cd2-123c-544a-8765-260ef74a7b42" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248634 1034 "\\frac{2a+3}{a-7}" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248634 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533725 true] [17592186248634 1111 #uuid "f356baed-6fb4-5c7e-ad77-3beb19dc5ac6" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248635 1017 #edb/ref 17592186248636 13194139533725 true] [17592186248635 1089 "q-74721" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248635 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533725 true] [17592186248635 1100 "Find, in radians to two decimal places, the argument of $z=-5-6\\text{i}.$ \n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248635 1113 #uuid "7b9c4974-b912-58ae-8763-c4d9a8b6f790" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248635 1138 false 13194139533725 true] [17592186248635 1145 "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/assessment-13930620/assets/q-74721-e-0.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the third quadrant of the complex plane. Therefore $\\pi <arg(z)<\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$ If $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the negative real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha  & =arctan(\\frac{6}{5})\\approx 0.876\\,06.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg(z)\\approx \\pi +0.876\\,06\\approx 4.02\n$$\n\nto two decimal places." 13194139533725 true] [17592186248636 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248637 13194139533725 true] [17592186248636 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248638 13194139533725 true] [17592186248636 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248639 13194139533725 true] [17592186248636 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248640 13194139533725 true] [17592186248636 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248641 13194139533725 true] [17592186248636 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533725 true] [17592186248636 1041 "selection" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248636 1104 #edb/ref 17592186248639 13194139533725 true] [17592186248636 1110 #uuid "810e2725-192f-548b-ab0c-fb0a56f98ad5" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248637 1034 "2.40" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248637 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533725 true] [17592186248637 1111 #uuid "a297a75a-733b-5dba-b974-9ef20f006e25" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248638 1034 "0.42" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248638 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533725 true] [17592186248638 1111 #uuid "c2055bb3-cf46-5d8a-b8ca-46cac2194590" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248639 1034 "4.02" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248639 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533725 true] [17592186248639 1111 #uuid "f35f225f-00ba-5e03-ad2e-ae5b4f6dedca" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248640 1034 "4.20" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248640 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533725 true] [17592186248640 1111 #uuid "eccba0b4-a6a4-5015-9447-37e5af0060fa" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248641 1034 "2.04" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248641 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533725 true] [17592186248641 1111 #uuid "b2aa1a1e-e67d-52ef-a1d2-b0d082fb9bcd" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248642 1017 #edb/ref 17592186248643 13194139533725 true] [17592186248642 1089 "q-82938" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248642 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533725 true] [17592186248642 1100 "Which of the following diagrams shows a unit circle in the coordinate plane with a central angle of $-{53}^{\\circ }$ in the standard position?" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248642 1113 #uuid "6116f5ea-2ce3-56bf-80e5-593c2a7aeab6" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248642 1138 false 13194139533725 true] [17592186248642 1145 "Recall that:\n\n- A unit circle has a radius of $1$ and is centered at the origin in the coordinate plane.\n\n- An angle in the standard position has its initial side on the positive $x$-axis, its vertex is at the origin.\n\n- It rotates such that a positive angle is measured counter-clockwise, and a negative angle is measured clockwise.\n\nTherefore, the correct diagram is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/assessment-13930620/assets/q-82938-a-1.png)" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248643 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248644 13194139533725 true] [17592186248643 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248645 13194139533725 true] [17592186248643 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248646 13194139533725 true] [17592186248643 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248647 13194139533725 true] [17592186248643 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248648 13194139533725 true] [17592186248643 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533725 true] [17592186248643 1041 "selection" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248643 1104 #edb/ref 17592186248645 13194139533725 true] [17592186248643 1110 #uuid "b93523a3-0a58-5ba2-9618-0b6eda673103" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248644 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/assessment-13930620/assets/q-82938-a-2.png" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248644 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139533725 true] [17592186248644 1111 #uuid "c2ff1f9f-a136-5022-82e0-ed599d3d8865" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248645 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/assessment-13930620/assets/q-82938-a-1.png" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248645 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139533725 true] [17592186248645 1111 #uuid "5fd557be-a3db-5b00-ba31-e199cad38f9f" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248646 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/assessment-13930620/assets/q-82938-a-5.png" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248646 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139533725 true] [17592186248646 1111 #uuid "9129d971-de3e-53ad-ba29-f6537cd39e23" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248647 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/assessment-13930620/assets/q-82938-a-4.png" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248647 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139533725 true] [17592186248647 1111 #uuid "c906ae27-b4a6-577f-a9a1-f4e606d325fb" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248648 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/assessment-13930620/assets/q-82938-a-3.png" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248648 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139533725 true] [17592186248648 1111 #uuid "b7078933-d8af-5ff6-91a3-c345bcfa9afc" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248649 1017 #edb/ref 17592186248650 13194139533725 true] [17592186248649 1089 "q-98107" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248649 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533725 true] [17592186248649 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/assessment-13930620/assets/q-98107.png)\n\nWhat is the length of $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ in the diagram above?" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248649 1113 #uuid "603b28ad-abe0-56b9-9792-0364b2d44663" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248649 1138 false 13194139533725 true] [17592186248649 1145 "The length of $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ is equal to the distance between $P$ and $Q.$\n\nThe distance $d$ between two points $P({x}_{1},{y}_{1},{z}_{1})$ and $Q({x}_{2},{y}_{2},{z}_{2})$ is given by\n\n$$\nd=\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1}{)}^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1}{)}^{2}+({z}_{2}-{z}_{1}{)}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSince $P$ and $Q$ have coordinates ${{(-2,\\,-3,\\,-1)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{, }{y}_{1}\\text{, }{z}_{1}\\text{)}}$ and ${{(2,1,1)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{, }{y}_{2}\\text{, }{z}_{2}\\text{)}},$ respectively, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PQ & =\\sqrt{(2-(-2){)}^{2}+(1-(-3){)}^{2}+(1-(-1){)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248650 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248651 13194139533725 true] [17592186248650 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248652 13194139533725 true] [17592186248650 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248653 13194139533725 true] [17592186248650 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248654 13194139533725 true] [17592186248650 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248655 13194139533725 true] [17592186248650 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533725 true] [17592186248650 1041 "selection" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248650 1104 #edb/ref 17592186248654 13194139533725 true] [17592186248650 1110 #uuid "893b87d9-d065-5777-84a8-1b32df3a7c6c" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248651 1034 "12" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248651 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533725 true] [17592186248651 1111 #uuid "3d63294b-af29-5c27-a5fa-08a981e72a78" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248652 1034 "9" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248652 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533725 true] [17592186248652 1111 #uuid "f727672d-cda5-5acc-bca1-c2a127efe835" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248653 1034 "8" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248653 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533725 true] [17592186248653 1111 #uuid "6ec9e72c-bd7f-579f-9238-8206476d7f30" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248654 1034 "6" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248654 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533725 true] [17592186248654 1111 #uuid "a855376f-8ea0-5de5-aea5-40355f06d321" 13194139533725 true] [17592186248655 1034 "4" 13194139